# Build context for the published site only.
#
# The shared `.dockerignore` excludes `apps/web/` because the API and worker images must not ship a
# static front. This Dockerfile is the exception, so it carries its own ignore file: Docker uses
# `<Dockerfile>.dockerignore` when it exists, which keeps both intents without a negation hack.

# Everything a static build does not need.
.git/
node_modules/
**/node_modules/
**/dist/
**/coverage/
**/*.tsbuildinfo
*.log*
.env*
Dockerfile*
.dockerignore
.github/
.specify/
docs/
specs/
tests/
data/README.md

# Kept: the workspace manifests, `apps/web`, `packages/core` and the shared `data` reference.
!package.json
!pnpm-lock.yaml
!pnpm-workspace.yaml
!tsconfig.base.json
!tsconfig.json
!apps/web/
!packages/
!data/
# Only the static server config is read from infra/; the rest stays out of the context.
!infra/edge/web.conf
